ht"><h1>HTML Online Editor &amp; Compiler</h1>
<p>Write, Run &amp; Share HTML code online using OneCompiler's HTML online =
Code editor for free. It's one of the robust, feature-rich online Code edit=
or for HTML language, running on HTML5. Getting started with the OneCompile=
r's HTML compiler is simple and pretty fast. The editor shows sample boiler=
plate code when you choose language as <code node=3D"[object Object]">HTML<=
/code>. You can also specify the stylesheet information in <code node=3D"[o=
bject Object]">styles.css</code> tab and scripts information in <code node=
=3D"[object Object]">scripts.js</code> tab and start coding.</p>
<h1>About HTML</h1>
<p>HTML(Hyper Text Markup language) is the standard markup language for Web=
 pages, was created by Berners-Lee in the year 1991. Almost every web page =
over internet might be using HTML.</p>
<h1>Syntax help</h1>
<h2>Fundamentals</h2>
<ul>
<li>Any HTML document must start with document declaration <code node=3D"[o=
bject Object]">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</code></li>
<li>HTML documents begin with <code node=3D"[object Object]">&lt;html&gt;</=
code> and ends with <code node=3D"[object Object]">&lt;/html&gt;</code></li=
>
<li>Headings are defined with <code node=3D"[object Object]">&lt;h1&gt;</co=
de> to <code node=3D"[object Object]">&lt;h6&gt;</code> where <code node=3D=
"[object Object]">&lt;h1&gt;</code> is the highest important heading and <c=
ode node=3D"[object Object]">&lt;h6&gt;</code> is the least important sub-h=
eading.</li>
<li>Paragraphs are defined in <code node=3D"[object Object]">&lt;p&gt;..&lt=
;/p&gt;</code> tag.</li>
<li>Links are defined in <code node=3D"[object Object]">&lt;a&gt;</code> ta=
g.<!-- -->
<h4>Example:</h4>
<pre style=3D"background-color:#f5f5f5;padding:12px;border-radius:4px;overf=
low-x:auto"><code class=3D"plaintext hljs" node=3D"[object Object]">&lt;a h=
ref=3D"https://onecompiler.com/html"&gt;HTML online compiler&lt;/a&gt;
</code></pre>
</li>
<li>Images are defined in <code node=3D"[object Object]">&lt;img&gt;</code>=
 tag, where <code node=3D"[object Object]">src</code> attribute consists of=
 image name.</li>
<li>Buttons are defined in <code node=3D"[object Object]">&lt;button&gt;..&=
lt;/button&gt;</code> tag</li>
<li>Lists are defined in <code node=3D"[object Object]">&lt;ul&gt;</code> f=
or unordered/bullet list and <code node=3D"[object Object]">&lt;ol&gt;</cod=
e> for ordered/number list, and the list items are defined in <code node=3D=
"[object Object]">&lt;li&gt;</code>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>HTML Elements and Attributes</h2>
<ul>
<li>HTML element is everything present from start tag to end tag.</li>
<li>The text present between start and end tag is called HTML element conte=
nt.</li>
<li>Anything can be a tagname but it's preferred to put the meaningful titl=
e to the content present as tag name.</li>
<li>Do not forget the end tag.</li>
<li>Elements with no content are called empty elements.</li>
<li>Elements can have attributes which provides additional information abou=
t the element.</li>
<li>In the below example, href is an attribute and a is the tag name.<!-- -=
->
<h4>Example:</h4>
<pre style=3D"background-color:#f5f5f5;padding:12px;border-radius:4px;overf=
low-x:auto"><code class=3D"plaintext hljs" node=3D"[object Object]">&lt;a h=
ref=3D"https://onecompiler.com/html"&gt;HTML online compiler&lt;/a&gt;
</code></pre>
</li>
</ul>
<h2>CSS</h2>
<p>CSS(cascading style sheets) describes how HTML elements will look on the=
 web page like color, font-style, font-size, background color etc.</p>
<h3>Example:</h3>
<p>Below is a sample style sheet which displays heading in green and in Can=
dara font with padding space of 25px.</p>
<pre style=3D"background-color:#f5f5f5;padding:12px;border-radius:4px;overf=
low-x:auto"><code class=3D"css hljs" node=3D"[object Object]"><span class=
=3D"hljs-selector-tag">body</span> {
  <span class=3D"hljs-attribute">padding</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-number=
">25px</span>;
}
<span class=3D"hljs-selector-class">.title</span> {
